  "glossary": {
    "hardkill": [
      "minimal: 1-4 defender/Pavise PDT",
      "good: >6 PDT, with a mixture of CIWS and Flak"
    ],
    "softkill": [
      "minimal: a single vls-1 with chaff, the same vls is usually used to house the arming missile",
      "full: refer to a series of countermeasures that counter all form of missile seekers, these include:",
      "cmd \"ball jammer\" - E70 and J75",
      "chaff and it's better counterpart: EA99 for ANS (the latter requires a vls-2 to house)",
      "killjoy missiles",
      "and for OSP, the Blackjack EO Jammer",
      "Good: Good/better softkill falls between the last two - a ship with good softkill is expect to have a part of the full softkill equipment on top of the minimal vls-1. Multiple ships with \"good\" softkill are usually formed together in a fleet with complementing equipment to achieve full softkill as a group/pair."
    ],
    "Damage Control (DC)": [
      "Damage Control refers to the series of compartments responsible for providing Damage Control teams and restores to a ship. But for \"Good\"/\"Better\" DC, this can also include other compartments that gives buff to damage control teams, such as Damage Control Central and Small Workshop."
    ]
  }
